{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQRiTBRkze9a5YeKQ3ykzb","type":"tool_result","content":"usage: status.py [-h] [--backlog BACKLOG] [--json] [target]\n=== initiative ===\ntaskspec: unknown command 'initiative'\nTaskSpec — atomic contracts and native AI engineering toolkit\n\nUsage: taskspec [--json] [--dry-run] <command> [options]\n\n  init               creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\n  setup              none\n  demo               creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\n  example            writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\n  new                creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\n  plan               none\n  batch              creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  migrate            atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\n  validate           refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\n  dod                none\n  gate               executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n  handoff            stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\n  run                runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n  accept             executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n  author-doctor      none\n  holdout            seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\n  receipt            creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\n  eval-audit         uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\n  identity           init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\n  evidence           run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\n  bridge             export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\n  dsse               export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\n  mcp                read-only stdio server\n  mesh               optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n  ready              none\n  graph              none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n  status             none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n  lint               none\n  transition         changes lifecycle status and derived state\n  rebuild-state      rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\n  archive            moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\n  backup             writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\n  metrics            none\n  conformance        self-test uses disposable fixtures only","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63460af6-85b1-4ee1-9781-8ece24e10dc3","uuid":"b5ab72d5-cfc4-453a-aa73-8bc0c8e2fffc","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:28:04.385Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"usage: status.py [-h] [--backlog BACKLOG] [--json] [target]\n=== initiative ===\ntaskspec: unknown command 'initiative'\nTaskSpec — atomic contracts and native AI engineering toolkit\n\nUsage: taskspec [--json] [--dry-run] <command> [options]\n\n  init               creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\n  setup              none\n  demo               creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\n  example            writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\n  new                creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\n  plan               none\n  batch              creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  migrate            atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\n  validate           refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\n  dod                none\n  gate               executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n  handoff            stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\n  run                runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n  accept             executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n  author-doctor      none\n  holdout            seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\n  receipt            creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\n  eval-audit         uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\n  identity           init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\n  evidence           run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\n  bridge             export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\n  dsse               export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\n  mcp                read-only stdio server\n  mesh               optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n  ready              none\n  graph              none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n  status             none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n  lint               none\n  transition         changes lifecycle status and derived state\n  rebuild-state      rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\n  archive            moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\n  backup             writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\n  metrics            none\n  conformance        self-test uses disposable fixtures only","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
