{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DsqBAuxkpg1KChiDf6NyCg","type":"tool_result","content":"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN example=task-plan path=/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat fvp5a5et/.taskspec/authoring-scratch/policy-schema/example-task-plan.json action=created digest=sha256:d084798daa3b4ddfa63c37b12ec81d8d7dcc7939079f0e3b1dfc206eaa5cfd21\napi_version: taskspec.dev/v1\nkind: TaskPlan\napproved: true\nmetadata:\n  name: add-search-command\n  source: docs/runbooks/from-fuzzy-intent.md\nunits:\n  - id: T-20260811-add-search-command\n    title: Add a deterministic search command\n    effort: S\n    profile: standard\n    agent: any\n    execution_backend: codex\n    depends_on: []\n    touches_paths:\n      - bin/taskspec\n    creates_paths:\n      - tests/test-search-command.sh\n    source_note: docs/examples/task-plan.yaml\n    why: Users need a bounded example that demonstrates TaskPlan generation.\n    goal: Add a search command with a deterministic contract test.\n    context: Keep the command offline and do not add provider credentials.\n    behaviors:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a repository with Task-Spec installed\n        when: the user invokes the search command with a query\n        then: the CLI returns a deterministic local result or a named unavailable state\n    evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: the search command contract test passes\n        command: bash tests/test-search-command.sh\n        verifies:\n          - B-1\n        terminal: true\n        expected_duration_sec: 10\n    anti_patterns:\n      - Do not call an external provider unless the user explicitly selects one.\n    do_not_touch:\n      - tools/setup-taskspec-signing-key.sh","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63460af6-85b1-4ee1-9781-8ece24e10dc3","uuid":"4e9719b2-fc1f-4bb2-967a-c219267ba4c3","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:28:33.904Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN e