seconds window representation in (1) are the least grounded choices and are the ones most likely to change. The declared evals encode these proposals, so changing a decision means re-authoring this draft, not editing evals after sealing.\",\n      \"behaviors\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B-1\",\n          \"given\": \"a policy document declaring a supported schema_version with a valid limit and window\",\n          \"when\": \"validate_policy is called on it\",\n          \"then\": \"it returns valid true with an empty errors list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B-2\",\n          \"given\": \"a policy whose limit is zero, negative, above the maximum, a string, a float, or a bool\",\n          \"when\": \"validate_policy is called on it\",\n          \"then\": \"it returns valid false and an error with code invalid_limit naming the limit field, without raising\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B-3\",\n          \"given\": \"a policy whose window_seconds is zero, negative, above the maximum, a string, a float, or a bool\",\n          \"when\": \"validate_policy is called on it\",\n          \"then\": \"it returns valid false and an error with code invalid_window naming the window_seconds field, without raising\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B-4\",\n          \"given\": \"a policy whose schema_version is absent or is not in SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS\",\n          \"when\": \"validate_policy is called on it\",\n          \"then\": \"it returns valid false with code missing_field when absent and unsupported_schema_version when unrecognized, and does not fall back to a default version\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B-5\",\n          \"given\": \"a policy that is not a mapping, or a mapping with several independent faults\",\n          \"when\": \"validate_policy is called on it\",\n          \"then\": \"it returns valid false reporting every applicable error code rather than raising or stopping at the first fault\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"evals\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"eval_1\",\n          \"description\": \"Contract test for the policy schema passes\",\n          \"command\": \"bash tests/test-policy-schema.sh\",\n          \"verifies\": [\"B-1\", \"B-2\", \"B-3\", \"B-4\", \"B-5\"],\n          \"terminal\": true,\n          \"expected_duration_sec\": 20\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"eval_2\",\n          \"description\": \"Discrimination check run directly against the module API, not through the task-authored test file: an accept-everything stub, a reject-everything stub, and a stub that raises on malformed input all fail this eval\",\n          \"command\": \"python3 -c 'import sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"src\\\")\\nfrom rate_limiting.policy_schema import validate_policy, SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS\\nassert \\\"1.0.0\\\" in SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS, SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS\\nassert \\\"0.9.0\\\" not in SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS, SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS\\ngood = {\\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 100, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 60}\\nres = validate_policy(good)\\nassert res[\\\"valid\\\"] is True and res[\\\"errors\\\"] == [], res\\nassert validate_policy({**good, \\\"limit\\\": 1})[\\\"valid\\\"] is True\\nassert validate_policy({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 86400})[\\\"valid\\\"] is True\\ncases = [({**good, \\\"limit\\\": 0}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"limit\\\": -1}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"limit\\\": 1000001}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"limit\\\": \\\"100\\\"}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"limit\\\": 100.0}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"limit\\\": True}, \\\"invalid_limit\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 0}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": -60}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 86401}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": \\\"60\\\"}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 60.0}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"window_seconds\\\": False}, \\\"invalid_window\\\"), ({**good, \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"0.9.0\\\"}, \\\"unsupported_schema_version\\\"), ({\\\"limit\\\": 100, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 60}, \\\"missing_field\\\"), (None, \\\"invalid_policy\\\"), ([], \\\"invalid_policy\\\")]\\nfor policy, code in cases:\\n    res = validate_policy(policy)\\n    assert res[\\\"valid\\\"] is False, (\\\"accepted invalid policy\\\", policy, res)\\n    codes = [e[\\\"code\\\"] for e in res[\\\"errors\\\"]]\\n    assert code in codes, (\\\"expected\\\", code, \\\"for\\\", policy, \\\"got\\\", res)\\nmulti = validate_policy({\\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"0.9.0\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 0, \\\"window_seconds\\\": 0})\\nassert set(c for c in (e[\\\"code\\\"] for e in multi[\\\"errors\\\"])) >= {\\\"unsupported_schema_version\\\", \\\"invalid_limit\\\", \\\"invalid_window\\\"}, multi\\nprint(\\\"POLICY_SCHEMA_DISCRIMINATION=OK\\\")'\",\n          \"verifies\": [\"B-1\", \"B-2\", \"B-3\", \"B-4\", \"B-5\"],\n          \"terminal\": true,\n          \"expected_duration_sec\": 20\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"eval_3\",\n          \"description\": \"The evidence fixture is unmodified and no rate-limiting behavior beyond validation was added\",\n          \"command\": \"python3 -c 'import hashlib, pathlib, sys\\np = pathlib.Path(\\\"tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\\\")\\nd = hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\\nassert d == \\\"f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\\\", (\\\"blueprint fixture modified\\\", d)\\nsrc = pathlib.Path(\\\"src/rate_limiting/policy_schema.py\\\").read_text()\\nfor banned in (\\\"import requests\\\", \\\"import sqlite3\\\", \\\"open(\\\", \\\"socket\\\", \\\"time.sleep\\\"):\\n    assert banned not in src, (\\\"out-of-scope dependency or side effect\\\", banned)\\nprint(\\\"POLICY_SCHEMA_SCOPE=OK\\\")'\",\n          \"verifies\": [\"B-1\"],\n          \"terminal\": false,\n          \"expected_duration_sec\": 10\n        }\n      ],\n      \"anti_patterns\": [\n        \"Do not implement policy resolution, request counting, denial reasons, or decision telemetry; those are steel thread steps 2 to 4 and are separate leaves.\",\n        \"Do not raise on malformed input as the rejection mechanism; callers in later steps need a structured result.\",\n        \"Do not default a missing or unrecognized schema_version to the latest supported version.\",\n        \"Do not add a third-party validation dependency; the standard library is sufficient for this shape.\",\n        \"Do not treat bool as a valid integer for limit or window_seconds.\"\n      ],\n      \"do_not_touch\": [\n        \"tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\",\n        \".taskspec/\",\n        \"AGENTS.md\",\n        \"CLAUDE.md\"\n      ],\n      \"rollback\": \"Delete src/rate_limiting/ and tests/test-policy-schema.sh; the task creates only new files and touches no existing ones.\",\n      \"sdlc_stages\": [\"build\", \"test\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":7,"newStart":25,"newLines":7,"lines":["       \"why\": \"Steel thread step 1 of the rate-limiting blueprint. Every later step (policy resolution, the 101st-request denial, denial telemetry) reads a policy; without a versioned schema that rejects invalid limits and windows, those steps would have to re-validate input and would inherit malformed policies.\",","       \"goal\": \"Add a versioned rate-limit policy schema module that validates a policy document, accepts a well-formed policy, and rejects invalid limits, invalid windows, and unsupported schema versions with named, machine-readable error codes instead of raised exceptions.\",","       \"done_condition\": \"src/rate_limiting/policy_schema.py exposes SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS and validate_policy(policy) -> {\\\"valid\\\": bool, \\\"errors\\\": [{\\\"code\\\": str, \\\"field\\\": str}]}, all declared evals pass, and the blueprint fixture is unchanged.\",","-      \"context\": \"This repository currently has no rate-limiting source; this task creates the first module of it under src/rate_limiting/. Python 3 and bash are available and no third-party dependency may be added. Scope is validation of a single policy document in memory: no storage, no provider metering, no resolution of which policy applies to an organization, no counting, and no telemetry. OPEN DECISIONS - the blueprint states that the schema is versioned and rejects invalid limits and windows, but does not state the concrete contract. The following are PROPOSED by this draft and must be confirmed or replaced at review before the task is sealed: (1) policy shape {schema_version, limit, window_seconds}; (2) SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS == {\\\"1.0.0\\\"}; (3) limit must be a non-bool int with 1 <= limit <= 1000000; (4) window_seconds must be a non-bool int with 1 <= window_seconds <= 86400; (5) error codes invalid_limit, invalid_window, unsupported_schema_version, missing_field, and invalid_policy for a non-mapping input; (6) a missing schema_version is reported as missing_field. The upper bounds in (3) and (4) and the fixed-seconds window representation in (1) are the least grounded choices and are the ones most likely to change. The declared evals encode these proposals, so changing a decision means re-authoring this draft, not editing evals after sealing.\",","+      \"context\": \"This repository currently has no rate-limiting source; this task creates the first module of it under src/rate_limiting/. Python 3 and bash are available and no third-party dependency may be added. src/rate_limiting is an implicit namespace package; do not add __init__.py, so the write surface stays at the two declared files. Scope is validation of a single policy document in memory: no storage, no provider metering, no resolution of which policy applies to an organization, no counting, and no telemetry. OPEN DECISIONS - the blueprint states that the schema is versioned and rejects invalid limits and windows, but does not state the concrete contract. The following are PROPOSED by this draft and must be confirmed or replaced at review before the task is sealed: (1) policy shape {schema_version, limit, window_seconds}; (2) SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSIONS == {\\\"1.0.0\\\"}; (3) limit must be a non-bool int with 1 <= limit <= 1000000; (4) window_seconds must be a non-bool int with 1 <= window_seconds <= 86400; (5) error codes invalid_limit, invalid_window, unsupported_schema_version, missing_field, and invalid_policy for a non-mapping input; (6) a missing schema_version is reported as missing_field. The upper bounds in (3) and (4) and the fixed-seconds window representation in (1) are the least grounded choices and are the ones most likely to change. The declared evals encode these proposals, so changing a decision means re-authoring this draft, not editing evals after sealing.\",","       \"behaviors\": [","         {","           \"id\": \"B-1\","]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
