 The concrete schema contract (policy shape, supported version set, limit and window bounds, error-code names) is proposed here, not stated by the blueprint; see Open Questions. Confirm or replace those decisions at review before sign-off.\"'),\n ('execution_backend: any', 'execution_backend: any'),\n ('# \"{{TODO: one-line title in imperative voice}}\"',\n  '# \"Add a versioned rate-limit policy schema that rejects invalid limits and windows\"'),\n ('> **Why:** {{TODO: 1-2 sentence why}}',\n  '> **Why:** Steel thread step 1 of the rate-limiting blueprint. Every later step — policy\\n> resolution, the 101st-request denial, denial telemetry — reads a policy, so without a\\n> versioned schema that rejects invalid limits and windows each of those steps would have\\n> to re-validate its input and would otherwise inherit malformed policies.'),\n]\nfor a,b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a,b,1)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"frontmatter+header done\")\nPY","description":"Fill frontmatter and header"}}}
