{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf6LYgkeWfLGDC88EukUW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Authored and validated. Nothing implemented, authorized, or accepted.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`tasks/T-20260915-rate-limit-policy-schema.md` — one atomic leaf, `status: blocked`, `signed_off: false`, `accepted: false`.\n\nScope is **steel thread step 1 only** (\"a versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows\"). Steps 2–4 from the blueprint (resolving one effective policy per org, denying request 101, stable denial reason + telemetry) are named in the spec as separate downstream leaves, not folded in. Write surface is two new files (`src/rate_limiting/policy_schema.py`, `tests/test-policy-schema.sh`), no existing file modified.\n\n## Acceptance checks — executed to prove they discriminate\n\nThree runnable bash evals, 6 behaviors, traceability closed both ways (`taskspec dod` → `DOD=COMPLETE`).\n\n| variant under test | eval_2 (API discrimination) | eval_3 (purity + fixture) |\n|---|---|---|\n| accept-everything stub | fail | pass |\n| reject-everything stub | fail | pass |\n| raises-on-malformed stub | fail | pass |\n| correct reference impl | **pass** | **pass** |\n| impl that mutates caller's policy | pass | **fail** |\n\nCurrent repo, nothing built: `eval_1=1 eval_2=1 eval_3=1` — red before implementation, as it should be.\n\n`eval_2` deliberately runs against the module API rather than through `tests/test-policy-schema.sh`, so an executor cannot satisfy it by writing a lenient test file. `eval_3` pins the blueprint fixture digest (`f40ed16c…7af445`), so modifying the evidence source fails acceptance.\n\n`taskspec validate` → OK (v3, standard profile). `taskspec lint` → `LINT=OK`, `issues=0`. Authoring scratch removed.\n\n## What I need from you before this can be sealed\n\nThe blueprint says the schema is versioned and rejects invalid limits and windows, but never states the contract. I proposed one and recorded it as six open **review** decisions in the spec rather than encoding it as agreed requirement — that's why the spec is `blocked`, not `ready`. The two weakest:\n\n1. **Window representation** — I proposed `window_seconds: int`. Step 3 (\"request 101 denied in the same window\") may want `{unit, count}` instead. Worth settling against step 3 first.\n2. **Upper bounds** — `limit <= 1000000`, `window_seconds <= 86400` are invented guards with no source in the blueprint.\n\nThe evals encode these proposals, so changing one means re-authoring this spec — not editing evals after sealing.\n\nNext command is yours, not mine: `taskspec gate --stamp tasks/T-20260915-rate-limit-policy-schema.md --stamp-by <identity>` authorizes this exact revision. It will refuse while `status: blocked` stands, so resolve the decisions and flip status first. Files are untracked; I did not commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":61017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":343},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63460af6-85b1-4ee1-9781-8ece24e10dc3","uuid":"cf2eda3f-9da5-43f8-a322-0784cfaf2ec1","timestamp":"2026-09-16T02:34:55.024Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6LYgU24gHy1FhkZZSn7"}
